  "title": "Erdős Problem #865",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "There exists a constant $C>0$ such that, for all large $N$, if $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ has size at least $\\frac{5}{8}N+C$ then there are distinct $a,b,c\\in A$ such that $a+b,a+c,b+c\\in A$.",
